<title>USA: US FCC grants 73 licenses for Ka-Band satellites.</title>
<headline>US FCC grants 73 licenses for Ka-Band satellites.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Communications Commission Friday issued licenses to 13 companies for 73 satellites that will provide geostationary-orbit fixed satellite service in the Ka-band.</p>
<p>The companies that received licenses include PanAmSat Corp, Lockheed Martin Corp, Loral Space &amp; Communications Ltd, a subsidiary of Motorola Inc, General Motors Corp's Hughes Electronics Corp, and the GE American Communications Inc unit of General Electric Co.</p>
</text>
